---
source: crates/wolf_sema/tests/layout_diagnostics.rs
expression: "render_tc(\"struct Vec2 {\\n    x: f64,\\n    y: f64,\\n}\\n\\n\\\n             #[repr(c)]\\nstruct Wrap {\\n    tag: u8,\\n    v: Vec2,\\n}\\n\\n\\\n             fn main() -> !int {\\n    const S = size_of(Wrap)\\n    if S == 24 { 0 } else { 1 }\\n}\\n\")"
---
error[E0708]: the layout of `Vec2` (the field `Wrap.v`) is not resolved until codegen lays it out
  --> mem:///main.lu:13:15
   |
13 |     const S = size_of(Wrap)
   |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ unresolved until codegen
   |               ------------- while evaluating `main`, entered here
   |
   = note: `size_of`, `align_of` and `offset_of` answer at comptime for scalars and `#[repr(c)]`
     structs, whose layout the clause fixes ([abi.layout.query]); any other type has the
     native layout, which the code generator chooses ([abi.native.layout]) — mark the struct
     `#[repr(c)]` to make its layout a fact.
